<title>USA: U.S. says Chinese troop deployment not unusual.</title>
<headline>U.S. says Chinese troop deployment not unusual.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was not surprised by the announcement that China would send 4,000 troops into Hong Kong on July 1 soon after the British colony reverts to Chinese control, a White House official said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We understand that this is what was always expected, that they would be garrisoning up to 10,000 troops in Hong Kong, and this is the first wave,&quot; said the official, who spoke on condition of anonymity.</p>
</text>
